# PHASE 2: REMOVE DEMO DATA, IMPLEMENT REAL FUNCTIONALITY, AND POLISH THE EXPENSE TRACKER MVP

## 1. Mission and execution requirements

You are continuing development of an existing AI-powered Expense Tracker application.

The first development phase successfully established the main UI, dashboard, transaction history, trends page, authentication screen, AI Insights section, and basic interaction layouts. The visual foundation is acceptable for the current MVP and must be preserved.

However, the application still contains sample data, some nonfunctional controls, an incomplete light/dark theme implementation, and no verified working backend persistence.

Your responsibility is to transform the existing prototype into a clean, functional, data-driven MVP.

**Do not rebuild the application from scratch. Do not redesign the entire interface unnecessarily. Do not discard working components simply because you can generate replacements.**

Inspect the existing codebase, identify the actual causes of each issue, and modify the smallest appropriate set of components and services. Preserve the current visual identity, navigation, responsive layout, and useful functionality.

This is an implementation task, not a planning exercise. Make the changes directly in the existing project, run the application, verify the relevant workflows, and fix the errors you encounter.

The order of priorities is:

1. Remove all hardcoded and seeded financial data.
2. Implement genuine data persistence and user isolation.
3. Make light and dark modes work correctly.
4. Improve the monthly budget component.
5. implement safe transaction deletion.
6. Replace confusing financial terminology.
7. Audit every interactive control and verify its functionality.
8. Test the entire MVP and report remaining limitations honestly.

