## 3. Remove all sample data and establish a genuinely clean application

This is one of the highest-priority requirements.

The current application contains example transactions, financial summary values, chart data, and AI insight examples. These were useful during development, but they must not appear as actual financial records in the released MVP.

### Remove all seeded financial data

Remove development/demo records and hardcoded financial values from:

- Total Balance.
- Total Income.
- Total Expenses.
- Monthly spending and remaining budget.
- Recent Transactions.
- History.
- Expense category breakdowns.
- Income-versus-expense charts.
- Trend calculations.
- AI Insights.
- Month-over-month comparisons.
- Any other financial summaries or transaction lists.

Search the entire relevant codebase for hardcoded transaction objects, mock API responses, default transaction arrays, placeholder monetary values, example dates, and static financial insight strings.

Remove the source of the sample data rather than merely hiding it in the UI.

### New-user experience

When a genuinely new user signs in for the first time, their account must start with:

- No transactions.
- Total income of ₹0.
- Total expenses of ₹0.
- Net balance of ₹0, unless an explicitly supported opening-balance feature is configured.
- No fabricated historical trends.
- No fabricated category breakdown.
- No invented AI insights.
- No preloaded financial activity.

The monthly budget may initially be unset. If the interface needs a default budget, clearly distinguish that configured or default limit from actual spending and never present it as a transaction or an account balance.

### Empty states

Do not leave blank white spaces or broken charts when data is unavailable.

Use clear, friendly empty states, such as:

- "No transactions yet. Add your first income or expense to get started."
- "Your spending trends will appear here once you record transactions."
- "AI Insights will become available when there is enough spending data."
- "Set a monthly budget to start tracking your spending."

Provide relevant actions where appropriate, such as Add Expense, Add Income, or Set Budget.

Charts should display a sensible empty state instead of fake chart segments.

AI Insights must distinguish between insufficient data and a genuine finding.

### Existing user data

Do not indiscriminately delete existing users, authentication records, or database records merely to remove demo data.

If the current database contains identifiable development seed records, remove only those records through a safe, controlled migration or cleanup process.

Do not delete real user-created transactions.

If it is impossible to distinguish demo records from real records safely, explain the issue and preserve the data until a safe cleanup method is established.

