## 11. AI Insights must remain data-driven

Preserve the AI Insights section and its existing visual design.

The focus remains on expense analysis, including:

- Largest spending category.
- Category spending distribution.
- Weekday-versus-weekend spending using transaction dates.
- Month-over-month comparisons where sufficient historical data exists.
- Budget utilization and overspending warnings.
- Meaningful changes in spending patterns.

All monetary values, percentages, comparisons, and category rankings must be calculated from verified transaction data.

AI may summarize and explain these calculations, but it must not invent the underlying figures.

For an account with no transactions, display a friendly empty state instead of prewritten insights.

For an account with insufficient historical data, explain that more records are needed for comparisons.

When transactions change, invalidate or refresh stale insight results as appropriate.

Do not make an expensive AI request every time the user opens the dashboard if deterministic calculations can provide the same information. Use AI where interpretation genuinely adds value.

Keep AI API credentials secure.

